{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785185830,"nonce":"DNsyuY5fdWdi9qUqDo/0G5H3MDw=","title":"ADR-0062: Export mounts need redirect_dir=on, and the change-set reader must therefore SUPPORT redirect","message":"Two slices were specified so they disagree, and both are individually correct.\n\n`rename(2)` of a directory that exists only in the lower layer returns **EXDEV** inside an overlay without `redirect_dir=on` — measured: `rename failed: Cross-device link`, module default `N`. git, cargo, npm, pip and maven all rename directories, and these work today because `/workspace` is a plain `emptyDir`. So an Export **must** mount `redirect_dir=on`. Verified it coexists with `nfs_export=on` (unlike `metacopy`, which is refused as a conflicting option).\n\nWorse than an error: `mv` *masks* EXDEV by recursively copying the subtree, so the failure mode is a **silent full copy of an inherited tree** into the upper layer — which makes \"the change set is the upper layer, exactly\" re-ingest a tree that nothing changed.\n\nBut a directory rename under `redirect_dir=on` records the old path in `trusted.overlay.redirect`, and the change-set reader built in `cb53ca9` deliberately treats `redirect` as **unsupported and refuses loudly**. That refusal was the right call given what was known; with `redirect_dir=on` required, it would refuse on every renamed directory.\n\n\n- [ ] The change-set reader resolves `trusted.overlay.redirect` instead of refusing it: the upper path is not the merged path, and the change set must be expressed in merged-view terms\n- [ ] A directory rename produces a change set a drain can apply correctly — the old subtree gone, the new one present, with no re-ingest of unchanged content\n- [ ] Export mounts set `redirect_dir=on`, and the substrate check asserts the combination still mounts\n- [ ] A rename form that genuinely cannot be represented still fails loudly rather than silently dropping a path\n\n\n- cb53ca9 (s2)","files":null}]}